    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nIn my code, I would like to do infer return type of the regular function in the same way as in #7877\n```cython\ndef bar() -> list[int]:\n    return [2]\n\ndef main():\n    b = bar()\n    print(b[0])  # Here I want to have  __Pyx_GetItemInt_List() instead of __Pyx_GetItemInt()\n```\n\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like.\n\nI think same as in #7877\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered.\n\nI think same as in #7877\n\n### Additional context\n\nCurrently we do infer return value for `cdef` and `cpdef` function only.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "A couple of comments: \n* It's possible to monkey-patch regular `def` functions so you can't necessarily reason about exactly what's being called. It might be reasonable to assume the same signature though. \n* Decorators might be a complication. I think the signature would normally describe the wrapped function? Which isn't automatically the same as the wrapper function. Potentially this could be inferred too, but it's more involved. It might be better to ignore decorated functions initially",
